-- The DEFINITIONS for nlg-mixfix-import.l4, which calls them across an IMPORT.
-- The same shapes, in the same order, as nlg-mixfix-local.l4: see there for
-- why each is here.

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the smaller of %a% and %b%
`the lower of` a `and` b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount by which` a `exceeds` b @nlg the amount by which %a% exceeds %b%
  MEANS a MINUS b

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg %b% less %a%
`the shortfall of` a `against` b MEANS b MINUS a

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg %a% and %b% together
a `plus` b MEANS a PLUS b

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the first of %a%
`the first of` a `then` b MEANS a

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the bare` a `and` b MEANS a PLUS b

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the greater of %a% and %b%
`the greater` a b MEANS IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b
